# The build context is this add-on folder, not the repository. Everything that
# used to be listed here — web/, test/, tools/, fixtures/, branding/ — now lives
# beside the add-on rather than inside it, so it was never in the context to
# begin with and listing it only implied otherwise.

# Runtime state. The dev server writes a real house's plan here; Home Assistant
# mounts /data separately in production. It must never be baked into the image,
# and .gitignore keeps it out of the repository for the same reason.
app/data

# Documentation is read on GitHub and in the Home Assistant UI, not by the
# running process. SKILL.md is the exception: the MCP server serves that exact
# working guide from the image, so excluding it makes Dockerfile COPY fail.
*.md

# ...except the MCP guide and the notices, which the image is obliged to carry.
# LICENSE and NOTICE have no extension and were never matched by `*.md` above.
!SKILL.md
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
